To celebrate the one year aniversary of the Vulture's project[1],
Vulture's-2.0.0 has been released, to the day it's been one year
exactly since I decided to fork Falcon's Eye[2]. It's been an exciting
ride and I hope you all enjoy Vulture's 2 as much as the development
team has enjoyed making it.

Finally after the longest wait for any Vulture's release, the largest
change ever has been set free. The amount of changes implemented is
quite massive. Many new tiles, a whole new interface revamp, everything
has moved from 8bpp to 24bpp and several hundred other changes that can
all be viewed online in the live changelog[3].

Vulture's 2.0.0 contains 1112 code patches since Falcon's Eye 1.9.3 of
which an astounding 501 patches have been commited to the project since
1.11.2. This release has almost as much code and changes as all
previous releases combined.

Vulture's 2.0.0 would not have been possible without Daniel Thaler,
Karen Pease and all the contributers, no matter how large or small, on
the Vulture's mailing list[4]

This is a source code release.  Binary installs for windows and RPMs
will appear on the site as the build maintainers create them in the
next day or two.

Enjoy
